Subject: xca, lzx, huffman: keep decoding inside the input and output

Found by fuzzing the decompressors (build/wimboot/fuzz) with inputs as a
crafted boot.wim can deliver them:

- xca: the bit and byte readers did not check the end of the input, so
  a chunk read up to a few bytes past it (they now read zeroes there, and
  the existing end-of-stream checks still reject such a chunk), and a
  match could copy from before the start of the output buffer (rejected).
- lzx: a pretree "same length" run (code 19) took its delta code without
  checking it, giving a code length of up to 255; huffman_alphabet() then
  incremented a counter up to 255 entries past its 16-entry table, a
  write outside the decoder state on the stack. Such a code is rejected,
  and huffman_alphabet() rejects lengths over HUFFMAN_BITS.
- huffman: an empty alphabet decoded its two placeholder symbols from
  before the raw symbol table; they now decode as symbol 0 explicitly.

Valid streams decode exactly as before. beast-boot (build/wimboot/); to
be offered upstream.

---
--- a/src/xca.h
+++ b/src/xca.h
@@ -66,16 +66,24 @@
 }
 
 /** Get word from source data stream */
-#define XCA_GET16( src ) ( {			\
-	const uint16_t *src16 = src;		\
-	src += sizeof ( *src16 );		\
-	*src16; } )
+#define XCA_GET16( src, end ) ( {				\
+	const uint8_t *src16 = src;				\
+	uint16_t val16 = 0;					\
+	if ( ( src16 + 1 ) < ( const uint8_t * ) (end) )	\
+		val16 = ( src16[0] | ( src16[1] << 8 ) );	\
+	else if ( src16 < ( const uint8_t * ) (end) )		\
+		val16 = src16[0];				\
+	src += sizeof ( val16 );				\
+	val16; } )
 
 /** Get byte from source data stream */
-#define XCA_GET8( src ) ( {			\
-	const uint8_t *src8 = src;		\
-	src += sizeof ( *src8 );		\
-	*src8; } )
+#define XCA_GET8( src, end ) ( {				\
+	const uint8_t *src8 = src;				\
+	uint8_t val8 = 0;					\
+	if ( src8 < ( const uint8_t * ) (end) )			\
+		val8 = *src8;					\
+	src += sizeof ( val8 );					\
+	val8; } )
 
 /** XCA source data stream end marker */
 #define XCA_END_MARKER 256
